      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The new patch set handles the unsuccessful command status properly.\n\nI don\u0027t think this is completely solved, looking at the bug we where hitting `ASSERT(complete_view.IsValid());` which makes me think that we will only check the status if we have the correct return parameters, which I don\u0027t expect to happens with `Unknown HCI Command`\n\n\u003e Therefore, it is sensible to disable this feature on Android devices to reduce interference.\n\nYes but this comes with the tradeoff of adding a runtime flag, and let OEMs on Android control this behaviour and I don\u0027t think we want that as this means more possible configuration to test (controller A with flag On, controller A with flag Off, ... instead of just controller A). We should be able to deduce the support from the controller.",
